WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:05.280
Once upon a time, there was a boy who was&nbsp;
born into a family of simple tailors in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:10.200
middle of sub-Saharan Africa. The boy’s father&nbsp;
wanted him to continue the family business,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:15.660
but the boy wanted a better life and one night&nbsp;
decided to leave his home and go to Europe.

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:21.180
To cross the sea the boy built himself&nbsp;
a raft. But once he left the shore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:26.520
there was only a little wind and it didn’t&nbsp;
take long for his supplies to run out. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:31.860
there he was: hungry, and lonely, floating&nbsp;
in the middle of the mediterranean sea.

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:36.540
Imagine you live on the coast of&nbsp;
Southern Europe and one morning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:42.420
read about the boy's fate in a local&nbsp;
paper. Should you yourself try to save him?

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:50.760
Four influential philosophers — Aristotle, Mill,&nbsp;
Kant, and Nietzsche — can help us answer this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:54.720
and other difficult moral questions&nbsp;
with their respective theories.

